    (uuid 1a4a2f21-be7d-5e68-ae5b-58858fe4673d)
  )
  (text "NOTES\n1. Round PCB D45 mm, 2 layers, 1.6 mm. U1, RD1, C4, C5 on the top (room side); everything else on the bottom.\n2. RD1 (HLK-LD2410C) sits flat below U1, not stacked: header insulator on the PCB, antenna face up,\n   about 16 mm from the WiFi antenna zone. Solder the 5 pins from the bottom and trim them.\n3. LD2410C pin order seen on the antenna face with the pins at the top: TX RX OUT GND VCC.\n   Always check against the silkscreen of your module before soldering.\n4. Radar UART1: RADAR_TX -> IO10 (ESP RX), IO3 (ESP TX) -> RADAR_RX, RADAR_OUT -> IO1. 256000 baud 8N1.\n5. Flashing over UART0 pads RX0/TX0 (3.3 V USB-UART). Download mode: short IO9 to GND while tapping RST\n   (or EN to GND). Power from USB-C or the 3V3 pad, not both.\n6. USB-C is power only: CC1/CC2 each have their own 5.1k to GND. PTC + TVS on the 5 V input,\n   AP2112K-3.3 (600 mA) for the ESP32-C3; the radar runs from 5 V directly.\n7. Unused GPIO: IO0 IO4 IO5 IO6 IO7 IO18 IO19 (not routed on the PCB).\n8. H1/H2: M2 mounting holes, PCB only (no symbol). No copper or metal within 15 mm of the antenna." (at 241.3 172.72 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 5e683a4c-db65-53ee-bc9d-f3949833f3f9)
  )

